  "constraints": "* Input arrays/tensors are non-empty and well-formed\n* Floating point values are finite real numbers\n* Numerical operations must adhere to standard precision tolerances",
  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_groupby_basics(records: list, group_col: str, value_col: str) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **GroupBy Basics** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_groupby_basics(records: list, group_col: str, value_col: str) -> list:\n    df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n    g = df.groupby(group_col)[value_col].agg(['sum', 'mean', 'count']).reset_index()\n    out = [{'group': r[group_col], 'sum': round(float(r['sum']), 4), 'mean': round(float(r['mean']), 4), 'count': int(r['count'])} for _, r in g.iterrows()]\n    out.sort(key=lambda x: str(x['group']))\n    return out\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
